      <!-- 1. HOW TO USE THE CALCULATOR -->
      <h2>How to Use the Loan Amortization Schedule Calculator</h2>
      <p>
        Generating an accurate, period-by-period repayment breakdown is simple with our comprehensive tool:
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Select your loan type:</strong> Choose between General Loan, Home Loan, Car Loan, Auto Loan, or Commercial Loan.</li>
        <li><strong>Enter the total loan amount:</strong> Input the borrowed principal in Indian Rupees (₹).</li>
        <li><strong>Enter the annual interest rate:</strong> Provide the annual percentage rate (e.g. 8.5% p.a.).</li>
        <li><strong>Select the loan term:</strong> Input your tenure in years or months, or click any of the 1-click quick tenure buttons.</li>
        <li><strong>Choose the payment frequency:</strong> Pick Monthly (12 payments/year), Biweekly (26 payments/year), or Weekly (52 payments/year).</li>
        <li><strong>Add the loan start date:</strong> Set the starting month and year to map repayment calendar dates.</li>
        <li><strong>Enter optional extra payments:</strong> Add regular extra principal contributions, an annual bonus payment, or a one-time lump sum.</li>
        <li><strong>Click Calculate Amortization Schedule:</strong> View your estimated payment, total interest, and payoff date.</li>
        <li><strong>Review the payment summary:</strong> Inspect the total cost of credit and interest-to-principal ratio.</li>
        <li><strong>Check the principal and interest breakdown:</strong> Visualize how each installment chips away at debt.</li>
        <li><strong>Switch between Yearly Summary and Detailed Schedule:</strong> View high-level annual rollups or full period-by-period ledger tables.</li>
        <li><strong>Download the selected schedule as a PDF:</strong> Save a branded PDF report for your personal budgeting or lender discussions.</li>
      </ol>

      <!-- 2. LOAN AMORTIZATION SCHEDULE EXAMPLE -->
      <h2>Loan Amortization Schedule Example</h2>
